# CLI acceptance — upstream catalog ingestion (`qai quran catalog`).
#
# Metadata-only: parses a local `editions.json` into edition records without
# touching the database or importing any text. Licences stay unknown.

```console
$ qai quran catalog tests/quran/fixtures/editions-mini.json
catalog: tests/quran/fixtures/editions-mini.json
entries: 2 (quran_text: 1, translation: 1, transliteration: 0, tafsir: 0, reference: 0, checksum: 0)
named transmissions: 1
  ara-quranuthmanihaf: hafs (inferred-from-upstream-name:uthmanihaf)
revision: unpinned
licenses: all unknown (redistribution not verified)

```

```console
$ qai quran catalog tests/quran/fixtures/editions-mini.json --revision 47ca096b0976443ba2eab2e45cdf0fb4096a2610
catalog: tests/quran/fixtures/editions-mini.json
entries: 2 (quran_text: 1, translation: 1, transliteration: 0, tafsir: 0, reference: 0, checksum: 0)
named transmissions: 1
  ara-quranuthmanihaf: hafs (inferred-from-upstream-name:uthmanihaf)
revision: 47ca096b0976443ba2eab2e45cdf0fb4096a2610
licenses: all unknown (redistribution not verified)

```

A missing file is a usage error; the database is never opened.

```console
$ qai quran catalog tests/quran/fixtures/does-not-exist.json
? 2
error: cannot read manifest `tests/quran/fixtures/does-not-exist.json`: [..]

```
